WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:01.240
November?

00:00:01.560 --> 00:00:02.580
More like New-vember...

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:03.640
Neflix-vember...

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:04.960
New-on-Neflix-vember?

00:00:05.380 --> 00:00:09.800
Whatever you want to call it, November 2019
is quickly approaching, and Netflix has announced

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:13.040
the movies and TV shows that will be available
to watch throughout the month.

00:00:13.300 --> 00:00:16.360
Here's the best stuff hitting Netflix in November
2019.

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.900
Netflix subscribers with a love for stand-up
will be treated in a major way, as the streamer

00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:24.700
is adding four specials from some of the biggest
names in comedy.

00:00:25.380 --> 00:00:30.279
On November 5, tuck into Seth Meyers' stand-up
comedy special Lobby Baby, in which the late-night

00:00:30.279 --> 00:00:34.340
host discusses everything from being a father
to the reason why "you should never take your

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:36.300
girlfriend to Paris for her birthday."

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:41.620
Filmed at Minneapolis' Pantages Theater, Seth
Meyers: Lobby Baby is extra-special for two

00:00:41.620 --> 00:00:42.120
reasons.

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.300
First, it's Meyers' first-ever Netflix comedy
special.

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:50.410
And second, it takes its name from the circumstances
of the birth of his second son, Axel Strahl

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:53.740
Meyers, who came into the world in the lobby
of Meyers' apartment building.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:58.560
A week later, on November 12, Jeff Garlin:
Our Man in Chicago hits Netflix.

00:00:58.680 --> 00:01:00.920
This special is, well, special too.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:05.600
It was filmed in Garlin's hometown of Chicago
37 years to the day after he debuted as a

00:01:05.619 --> 00:01:10.130
stand-up comedian, and it sees the Curb Your
Enthusiasm actor take a stroll down memory

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:14.240
lane that's filled with his, quote, "signature
blend of storytelling and improv."

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:19.140
Iliza Shlesinger's fifth Netflix stand-up
special, Unveiled, will arrive on the platform

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:20.140
on November 19.

00:01:20.440 --> 00:01:28.200
Following after 2013's War Paint, 2015's Freezing
Hot, 2016's Confirmed Kills, and 2018's Elder

00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:32.689
Millennial, Unveiled sees the recently-married
Shlesinger discuss all things wedding related,

00:01:32.689 --> 00:01:35.560
plus the, quote, "dangers of a zombie bachelorette
army."

00:01:35.760 --> 00:01:40.640
Finally, on November 26, Mike Birbiglia: The
New One will be available to stream on Netflix.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.260
In his newest stand-up special, Birbiglia
ponders whether he's truly ready to expand

00:01:45.260 --> 00:01:48.709
his family and bring a child into the often-terrifying
modern world.

00:01:49.709 --> 00:01:53.789
Do you like action franchises, iconic Will
Smith and Martin Lawrence movies from the

00:01:53.789 --> 00:01:57.040
'90s, classic Bruce Lee martial arts films,
and sequels?

00:01:57.360 --> 00:02:02.140
While we'd say you have quite a specific taste
in cinema, Netflix would say it has you covered.

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:14.819
Coming to Netflix in November 2019 are a handful
of awesome action flicks like 1995's Bad Boys,

00:02:14.819 --> 00:02:19.010
featuring Smith and Lawrence as a pair of
Miami detectives looking into the disappearance

00:02:19.010 --> 00:02:20.680
of police-seized drugs.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:25.420
You'll also be able to catch 1973's Enter
the Dragon, the beloved actioner from director

00:02:25.430 --> 00:02:29.780
Robert Clouse that marked Lee's final film
role before his death, all three entries in

00:02:29.780 --> 00:02:34.780
the Wachowskis' Matrix trilogy, and 2017's
Jumanji: Welcome to the Jungle, a follow-up

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:37.420
to the fantasy-adventure Jumanji from 1995.

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:43.040
Anyone who likes to expand spooky season into
November will be in luck next month on Netflix,

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:45.680
as three extra-eerie flicks are hitting the
streamer.

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.840
On the first day of the month, load up Roman
Polanski's seminal psychological horror feature

00:02:49.849 --> 00:02:54.860
Rosemary's Baby, starring Mia Farrow as the
titular Rosemary, a pregnant woman who grows

00:02:54.860 --> 00:02:59.200
suspicious that a Satanic coven wants to steal
her baby for use in their evil rituals.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.840
"What have you done to it?

00:03:03.340 --> 00:03:05.040
What have you done to its eyes?"

00:03:05.740 --> 00:03:10.890
On November 4, switch gears to District 9,
the Neill Blomkamp directed sci-fi action-thriller

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:15.189
that takes place in a South African internment
camp known as District 9, where insectoid

00:03:15.189 --> 00:03:17.580
aliens that crashed onto Earth have been confined.

00:03:17.909 --> 00:03:23.100
A bit later, on November 15, stream Netflix's
original thriller Earthquake Bird, a Tokyo-set

00:03:23.110 --> 00:03:28.060
mystery centered around expat Lucy Fly, the
reasons why she's suspected of killing her

00:03:28.060 --> 00:03:32.240
missing friend Lily, and the charming photographer
she was romantically involved with.

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:37.220
Escape the drama of your everyday life by
diving into the immersive, already-critically

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:39.080
acclaimed dramas heading to Netflix.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.340
The first arrival, hitting the streamer on
November 1, is The King.

00:03:42.680 --> 00:03:47.120
Based on a number of plays from William Shakespeare's
"Henriad" collection, The King tells the story

00:03:47.120 --> 00:03:51.410
of a prince who rises to take the English
Throne and become King Henry V, following

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:52.380
the death of his father.

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:54.460
"A king has no friends.

00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.240
Only followers.

00:03:58.220 --> 00:03:58.860
And foe."

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:04.200
The film opened in theaters for a limited
run on October 11, when critics took a liking

00:04:04.200 --> 00:04:04.740
to it.

00:04:04.960 --> 00:04:09.659
November 27 will see the Netflix debut of
Martin Scorsese's The Irishman, a gangster

00:04:09.659 --> 00:04:14.129
epic that chronicles the life and crimes of
Frank "The Irishman" Sheeran, a former mobster

00:04:14.129 --> 00:04:17.900
and hitman long presumed to have had a hand
in the disappearance and suspected killing

00:04:17.900 --> 00:04:19.530
of Teamster member Jimmy Hoffa.

00:04:19.980 --> 00:04:24.640
"Back then, there was nobody in this country
who didn't know who Jimmy Hoffa was."

00:04:24.960 --> 00:04:29.000
Like The King, The Irishman will have a limited
theatrical release prior to premiering on

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:29.820
Netflix.

00:04:30.060 --> 00:04:33.500
Critics have been praising The Irishman since
it debuted at the New York Film Festival on

00:04:33.500 --> 00:04:38.080
September 27, but audiences will have to wait
until November 1 to judge it for themselves,

00:04:38.320 --> 00:04:41.180
then hold out a few weeks until it's available
on Netflix.

00:04:41.380 --> 00:04:45.870
Those looking for non-Netflix-original dramas
can dig into David Ayer's End of Watch on

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.740
November 23, or Ridley Scott's All the Money
in the World on November 30.

00:04:50.580 --> 00:04:53.440
Christmas will come early for comedy-lovers
this November.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:57.740
On the first, Netflix is adding to its content
catalogue a number of hilarious movies like

00:04:57.740 --> 00:05:02.310
Step Brothers and Wedding Crashers, the witty
post-apocalyptic flick Zombieland, and even

00:05:02.310 --> 00:05:05.820
the subversive black comedy satire Fear and
Loathing in Las Vegas.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.120
"Whoa…

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:11.920
These fellas really let themselves go."

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.500
Later in the month, Netflix is really rolling
into the holiday spirit.

00:05:15.920 --> 00:05:18.480
On November 8, subscribers can stream Let
It Snow.

00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.300
Based on the New York Times bestseller, the
film follows a group of high school students

00:05:22.300 --> 00:05:24.960
as their lives cross paths during a Christmas
Eve snowstorm.

00:05:25.400 --> 00:05:26.780
"Snow hides a lot.

00:05:27.080 --> 00:05:28.700
It's like the Spanx of weather."

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:33.820
When November 15 rolls around, Netflix will
add animated comedy Klaus to its library,

00:05:33.820 --> 00:05:36.460
followed by The Knight Before Christmas on
November 21.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:41.220
This Vanessa Hudgens-starring flick sees science
teacher Brooke fall for Sir Cole, a medieval

00:05:41.220 --> 00:05:44.400
knight transported to the present day by a
mystical sorceress.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.660
Netflix sure didn't forget about TV enthusiasts,
though.

00:05:48.040 --> 00:05:51.720
The streamer is bringing a ton of amazing
short-form content to subscribers' screens

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:52.220
in November.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.620
On November 1, you can stream the Netflix
original event American Son, which follows

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:59.420
a mother as she pieces together the disappearance
of her son.

00:05:59.789 --> 00:06:04.460
Other stand-out TV additions include the third
season of Atypical and the Queer Eye special

00:06:04.460 --> 00:06:06.340
We're in Japan! on November 1.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:11.120
"I cannot wait to roll up our gorgeous little
gay sleeves and get this ball rolling."

00:06:11.440 --> 00:06:15.379
The second season of The End of the F***ing
World and the fourth season of She-Ra and

00:06:15.379 --> 00:06:19.400
the Princesses of Power hit the platform on
November 5, while the fifth volume of Patriot

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:23.780
Act with Hasan Minhaj premieres on November
10, and the third season of The Crown a week

00:06:23.780 --> 00:06:25.420
later, on November 17.

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:29.860
Netflix also has a few holiday TV specials,
like season 2 of The Great British Baking

00:06:29.860 --> 00:06:33.670
Show: Holiday Special on November 8 and season
2 of Nailed It!

00:06:33.670 --> 00:06:35.040
Holiday on November 22.

00:06:35.920 --> 00:06:37.960
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:06:38.060 --> 00:06:41.120
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
stuff are coming soon.

00:06:41.360 --> 00:06:44.620
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

